From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m5-i2s: consume RX PCM only after descriptor transfer

A guest RX descriptor is often smaller than the 4096-byte host staging
buffer. Advancing by the staging length discarded untransferred samples
on every DMA completion and changed the recorded tone's frequency. Keep
the source cursor at the number of bytes actually copied, including zero
on a failed/no-progress transfer and wrapping only at source EOF.

diff --git a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_i2s.c b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_i2s.c
index b3105de6..051ee1ed 100644
--- a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_i2s.c
+++ b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5_i2s.c
@@ -252,9 +252,14 @@ static void i2s_rx_timer(void *opaque)
     }
     chunk = MIN(available, sizeof(buffer));
     memcpy(buffer, s->rx_pcm + s->rx_pcm_pos, chunk);
-    s->rx_pcm_pos = (s->rx_pcm_pos + chunk) % s->rx_pcm_size;
     sent = esp_gdma_complete_in_descriptor(
         s->gdma, s->rx_dma_channel, buffer, chunk);
+    /* The descriptor can be shorter than the staging buffer, or fail before
+     * accepting any bytes. Consume only the bytes actually written to RAM so
+     * the next descriptor continues this PCM stream without dropping samples.
+     * At source EOF the next callback resumes from byte zero.
+     */
+    s->rx_pcm_pos = (s->rx_pcm_pos + sent) % s->rx_pcm_size;
     if (s->trace) {
         fprintf(stderr, "[i2s%d] rx dma inject chan=%u bytes=%u\n",
                 s->port, s->rx_dma_channel, sent);
